    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4e6010fce13349368b8d6579769cf54e",
      "statement": "llm-pi-ai is the pi-ai-backed multi-provider adapter: one plugin instance owns a dictionary of provider routes each served through pi-ai, a route naming an installed pi-ai provider inherits its endpoint, wire protocol and model catalog as defaults, a route pi-ai does not ship is declared outright (an OpenAI-compatible gateway is configuration), profiles and credentials resolve per request over the settings and credential seams, and the plugin can mount dormant with zero routes.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/llm/llm-pi-ai/README.md#L10-L12",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:462081e6a4b2a31020b456a14babc235c4a0da6d772c364e40b14eeafcf7cb20:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_cdbbf5c40ed9448fa86a0aa0c7fafdba",
      "statement": "llm-retry is the retry executor for failed model requests: it applies each provider's resolved retry policy at the agent loop's open-step agent/request-error extension point, does not wrap the streaming call itself, makes retry scheduling durable by appending llm/retry events before waiting, and runs normal mode (bounded failure codes up to maxRetries with exponential backoff) or always mode (downstream recovery first, then every failure without an attempt limit).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/llm/llm-retry/README.md#L10-L12",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:11c1d32e6936c3073cc0f0be1be8da2039ad2286309a8480401c44c53bfd9495:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0b4db9731f944ce7a2bd1e07ce88c8ed",
      "statement": "token-meter is the replay-aware token measurement service: ctx.tokenMeter advances one isolated fold per session from the durable event log, measures current request and context pressure, prices a single message, uses a fixed heuristic for text and routes without image pricing, applies adapter-declared visual-token pricing when available, and reuses provider-reported usage only when the request envelope matches exactly.",
